s a concentration of its receivables and revenues with specific customers. As of June 30, 2024, three customers accounted for 18%, 15% and 10% of accounts receivable, respectively. As of June 30, 2025, one customer accounted for 11% of accounts receivable.","context":"3) Concentration risks","section":"Segment Reporting","block":1913,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-003011","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-09","reportDate":"2025-06-30","cik":"0001966750","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966750/000121390026003011/ea0264703-20f_zhibao.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/d3276e62efebafa5c64c28ad0266826b57994c02fe40c21f2cb43854ab56f67e.bin","sha256":"d3276e62efebafa5c64c28ad0266826b57994c02fe40c21f2cb43854ab56f67e"}},{"id":"52510e14c2e538a8e22bbbc3a64583629a46db246ab66bcd6987b64cccbdebde","quote":"For the fiscal year ended June 30, 2023, one customer accounted for 12% of revenues. For the fiscal year ended June 30, 2024, two customer accounted for 14% and 13% of revenues, respectively. For the fiscal year ended June 30, 2025, two customers accounted for 22% and 14% of revenues.","context":"Accounts receivable are typically unsecured and derived from goods sold and services rendered to customers that are located primarily in China, thereby exposed to credit risk. The risk is mitigated by the Company’s assessment of customers’ creditworthiness and its ongoing monitoring of outstanding balances. The Company has a concentration of its receivables and revenues with specific customers. As of June 30, 2024, three customers accounted for 18%, 15% and 10% of accounts receivable, respectively. As of June 30, 2025, one customer accounted for 11% of accounts receivable.","section":"Segment Reporting","block":1914,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-003011","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-09","reportDate":"2025-06-30","cik":"0001966750","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966750/000121390026003011/ea0264703-20f_zhibao.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/d3276e62efebafa5c64c28ad0266826b57994c02fe40c21f2cb43854ab56f67e.bin","sha256":"d3276e62efebafa5c64c28ad0266826b57994c02fe40c21f2cb43854ab56f67e"}},{"id":"0a98581eb10d0bca20acfb124e6c531dde2a561e3d751468d734e57063ad6072","quote":"As of June 30, 2024, one vendor accounted for 26% of accounts payable. As of June 30, 2025, one vendor accounted for 13% of accounts payable.","context":"For the fiscal year ended June 30, 2023, one customer accounted for 12% of revenues. For the fiscal year ended June 30, 2024, two customer accounted for 14% and 13% of revenues, respectively. For the fiscal year ended June 30, 2025, two customers accounted for 22% and 14% of revenues.","section":"Segment Reporting","block":1915,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-003011","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-09","reportDate":"2025-06-30","cik":"0001966750","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966750/000121390026003011/ea0264703-20f_zhibao.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/d3276e62efebafa5c64c28ad0266826b57994c02fe40c21f2cb43854ab56f67e.bin","sha256":"d3276e62efebafa5c64c28ad0266826b57994c02fe40c21f2cb43854ab56f67e"}},{"id":"4cad2aae2b9a32e90fd453e006f0721070412faf035baece98bbfcf574d98d06","quote":"F-20","context":"As of June 30, 2024, one vendor accounted for 26% of accounts payable. As of June 30, 2025, one vendor accounted for 13% of accounts payable.","section":"Segment Reporting","block":1916,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001213900-26-003011","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-09","reportDate":"2025-06-30","cik":"0001966750","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1966750/0001213900260